INSERT INTO public."TestsData" ("TestId", "Questions", "Options", "Answers")
VALUES (460009382602015, ARRAY['"[8 marks] In a practical situation within “Project Development”, how should Ecnonomic Factors be applied? Explain the method, identify governing conditions and justify the expected result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] In a practical situation within “Process Design”, how should Continous v/s Batch Processing be applied? Explain the method, identify governing conditions and justify the expected result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] In a practical situation within “Project Development”, how should Objective of plant Project be applied? Explain the method, identify governing conditions and justify the expected result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] In a practical situation within “Project Development”, how should Pilot plant formation be applied? Explain the method, identify governing conditions and justify the expected result."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Ecnonomic Factors is listed under “Project Development” in the syllabus. Define it, explain its role and main process/design steps, relate it to Project Development, Objective of plant Project, Process evoluation stages and their importance, Pilot plant formation, and apply it to a chemical-engineering operation or equipment decision. State relevant assumptions or variables and explain how to verify the result and one limitation.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order, connect it to Project Development; Objective of plant Project; Process evoluation stages and their importance; Pilot plant formation, and identify relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units where calculations apply.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete CHEMICAL ENGINEERING PLANT ECONOMICS process, equipment or design question within “Project Development”. State the expected outcome and why the selected method fits.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective and note a source of error, safety concern or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Check technical details against official course material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Continous v/s Batch Processing is listed under “Process Design” in the syllabus. Define it, explain its role and main process/design steps, relate it to Selection of Process, shift and operating Schedule, Types of flow diagrame, block diagrame, and apply it to a chemical-engineering operation or equipment decision. State relevant assumptions or variables and explain how to verify the result and one limitation.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order, connect it to Selection of Process; shift and operating Schedule; Types of flow diagrame; block diagrame, and identify relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units where calculations apply.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete CHEMICAL ENGINEERING PLANT ECONOMICS process, equipment or design question within “Process Design”. State the expected outcome and why the selected method fits.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective and note a source of error, safety concern or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Check technical details against official course material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Objective of plant Project is listed under “Project Development” in the syllabus. Define it, explain its role and main process/design steps, relate it to Project Development, Process evoluation stages and their importance, Pilot plant formation, Techanical factors, and apply it to a chemical-engineering operation