on/example (2):** Apply it to a practical CHEMICAL ENGINEERING PLANT ECONOMICS problem and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result and state a limitation or risk.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning (2):** Selection of Process appears in “Process Design”. Define its purpose, explain the key steps or factors, connect it to Continous v/s Batch Processing, shift and operating Schedule, Types of flow diagrame, block diagrame, and give an applied example plus a check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Explain the topic and relate it to Continous v/s Batch Processing, shift and operating Schedule, Types of flow diagrame, block diagrame.\n\n**Application/example (2):** Apply it to a practical CHEMICAL ENGINEERING PLANT ECONOMICS problem and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result and state a limitation or risk.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning (2):** Selection of material and process equipments appears in “Selection Process Equipment and materials”. Define its purpose, explain the key steps or factors, connect it to selection of pumps and dryers., Selection Process Equipment and materials, and give an applied example plus a check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Explain the topic and relate it to selection of pumps and dryers., Selection Process Equipment and materials.\n\n**Application/example (2):** Apply it to a practical CHEMICAL ENGINEERING PLANT ECONOMICS problem and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result and state a limitation or risk.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

