VALUES (460009382601015, ARRAY['"[8 marks] In a practical situation within “Pressure Vessels”, how should Design criteria be applied? Explain the method, identify governing conditions and justify the expected result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] In a practical situation within “Basic Considerations in Process Equipment Design”, how should Fabrication Techniques be applied? Explain the method, identify governing conditions and justify the expected result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] In a practical situation within “Design Consideration”, how should Radiation effects be applied? Explain the method, identify governing conditions and justify the expected result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] In a practical situation within “Design Consideration”, how should Effects of fabrication methods Economic considerations. be applied? Explain the method, identify governing conditions and justify the expected result."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Pressure vessels contain pressurized fluids and require design consideration of pressure, temperature, materials, joints, corrosion and applicable codes.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order, connect it to Pressure Vessels; Operating conditions; Normal conditions; Transient conditions, and identify relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units where calculations apply.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete CHEMICAL PROCESS EQUIPMENT DESIGN process, equipment or design question within “Pressure Vessels”. State the expected outcome and why the selected method fits.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective and note a source of error, safety concern or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Check technical details against official course material."'::j