cedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order, connect it to Design Consideration; Material selection; Corrosion prevention; Stresses created due to static and dynamic loads, and identify relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units where calculations apply.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete CHEMICAL PROCESS EQUIPMENT DESIGN process, equipment or design question within “Design Consideration”. State the expected outcome and why the selected method fits.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective and note a source of error, safety concern or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Check technical details against official course material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Effects of fabrication methods Economic considerations. is listed under “Design Consideration” in the syllabus. Define it, explain its role and main process/design steps, relate it to Design Consideration, Material selection, Corrosion prevention, Stresses created due to static and dynamic loads, and apply it to a chemical-engineering operation or equipment decision. State relevant assumptions or variables and explain how to verify the result and one limitation.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order, connect it to Design Consideration; Material selection; Corrosion prevention; Stresses created due to static and dynamic loads, and identify relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units where calculations apply.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete CHEMICAL PROCESS EQUIPMENT DESIGN process, equipment or design question within “Design Consideration”. State the expected outcome and why the selected method fits.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1